// Task 178 LG, commit 3 (LG7): what each scenario of tests/diagnostic-log-migration.test.ts does at its call sites, in order.
//
// One line per call. "logDiagnostic" is the site's one logger call, entered when it is made, whatever the threshold
// is. Every other line is a call the site made before the migration and still makes: a Session Recording write, a
// trace store mutation, a human-evaluation call, a native command, a lifecycle authorization or a state update, with
// what it was given, or a marker the scenario itself enters ("native event", "enqueue", "listen", "store.content",
// "refs", "ready", "returned", "rethrown"). The error texts, device label, file path, transcript sentence and answer
// sentence in these lines are the planted inputs of the scenarios: they reach the recording, the trace store and the
// panel state as before. No log entry holds the provider error, the transcript or the answer; a path or a device
// label is in an entry only as part of the field `cause` (decisions A8), which is not in these lines.
//
// The table was taken from the migrated Hook on 2026-10-04 and compared, call by call, with the same scenarios run
// on the Hook and the trace store before the migration, where the logger calls were console calls: the other lines
// were identical, and each logger call sits where its console call sat. One logger call had no print before it: the
// trace store's "traces-cleared" after Debug Mode was turned off, which the Debug gate used to keep silent.
// "recordingClose" was added with decisions A8: the Hook had no print in that catch, its three logger lines are new,
// and its other lines are identical to the same scenario run on the Hook before the migration.
